        <p class="profile-detail-region">Life · Egypt &amp; North Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Ramesses II</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1303 BCE – 1213 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1303 BCE, into a family from the far north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nome">nome</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>; son of Seti I and grandson of Ramesses I, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> and military officer who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">1213 BCE (13 August by the most detailed reckoning; others give July or early August), aged about 90, most likely at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pi-ramesses">Pi-Ramesses</a>; cause unknown, possibly an infection from an abscess in the jaw</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">Prince regent under his father Seti I from about the age of fourteen; third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the Nineteenth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, 1279–1213 BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kadesh">Battle of Kadesh</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kadesh">Treaty of Kadesh</a>; the temples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-simbel">Abu Simbel</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesseum">Ramesseum</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>; the Delta capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pi-ramesses">Pi-Ramesses</a>; a 66-year reign with thirteen or fourteen Sed festivals; the Greek name Ozymandias</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="empire-meta">7 min read · Last reviewed October 2026</p>
      </div>
